From: Chaos Ruler <zmelumian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: clear slot hot-plug capability so the Root Port can enter D3

The Thor Root Port (17cb:0113) advertises SltCap HPC. With CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE
off, pci_bridge_d3_possible() returns false, the port stays in D0 in s2idle
("PCI PM: Skipped") and qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq() never powers the link down.
---
diff --color -ru a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c	2026-10-15 22:26:34.733796722 +0300
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c	2026-10-15 22:26:34.742393088 +0300
@@ -372,6 +372,16 @@
 	 */
 	val = readl(pci->dbi_base + offset + PCI_EXP_SLTCAP);
 	val |= PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_NCCS;
+	/*
+	 * Asgard: the slot is a soldered WCN7850, not hot-pluggable. Left
+	 * set, HPC makes the PCI core mark the Root Port is_pciehp, and
+	 * without native pciehp pci_bridge_d3_possible() refuses D3 for it.
+	 * The port then stays in D0 across system sleep, so
+	 * pci_host_common_d3cold_possible() fails and the link, controller
+	 * clocks, GDSC and PHY rails stay up. ponytail: unconditional, every
+	 * qcom PCIe on this kernel is soldered.
+	 */
+	val &= ~(PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_HPC | PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_HPS);
 	writel(val, pci->dbi_base + offset + PCI_EXP_SLTCAP);
 
 	dw_pcie_dbi_ro_wr_dis(pci);
